      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I've also noticed that video quality is noticeably worse on videos played in VRChat compared to just playing them normally in a web browser, despite having the settings for my map to play at 1080p. I also tried playing videos in other maps and noticed the same thing.\n\nFor example, here is an in-game VRChat screenshot playing a video that is just a still image and music: https://i.gyazo.com/be8b7b3f232b85f49710ae012d80b5fe.jpg\n\nHere is that same still image video as a screenshot taken from my browser: https://i.gyazo.com/8a0b03317093b28229d712c4b9c6e7eb.jpg\n\nDespite the video player settings being set to 1080p, it looks more like it's just defaulting to 360p in-game.\n\nThe list of issues with video players just keeps growing.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
