  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Video Players have always had issues but ever since the last patch they seem to have gotten even worse. I've posted about the issue with the video sync stream player causing infinite soft-crash loading screens for a lot of people (https://vrchat.canny.io/bug-reports/p/vrcsyncvideostream-locks-late-joiners-in-an-infinite-loading-screen) which I keep hearing about happening more lately. Not only that though, now there seems to be a new issue that is causing constant micro-stutters while watching a video, causing the video to desync way faster and also be a choppy viewing experience. Last night while trying to watch a movie with a bunch of people we first had issues using the video player (not the stream player at first) which was causing the audio of the movie to come out extremely choppy for everyone. After switching over to the stream player, this issue was fixed. However, it brought a new issue which was creating micro-stutters and sometimes split second load screens for over half the  people in the instance  every 3 seconds which was also causing more desync as a result. We then went to a different map, same issue. A third map, same issue. I thought maybe it was just the way I encoded and uploaded the video to Dropbox, but it's the same encoding I've always used without issues before and people in the room with me were reporting having similar issues with a different movie they tried watching earlier in the day. I've also heard more and more reports of the video players straight up crashing people when a video changes, although not sure if it's a literal hard game crash or a soft crash like what I described in my other canny post.\n\nEither way, video players right now have a plethora of issues with them and desperately need to be fixed. Please, please look into this already. These video players have had issues for months and now they're just getting worse, not better. I am tired of having to go through these types of issues constantly whenever I am trying to show a group of friends a movie.",
